  "body": "From https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/pull/2959#issuecomment-762636762:\r\n\r\n> Block widths are all over the place. Text blocks have one standard width, code blocks are wider, tables are sometimes wider, sometimes narrower than text, and so on. See section 12.11.1.6 for an example, where the two parameter tables (EncryptedFile and JWK) have different widths even though they are adjacent to each other. This sticks out like a sore thumb when scrolling through the document.",
